From 844ac922249089b87c0e88b613a97f5e4adc4d98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Lukens <jlukens@botch.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:15:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add optional RF listener support

A PLM hears only what reaches its own antenna. Battery devices (leak,
door, motion, remotes) are RF-only and can't be polled, so a message the
modem misses from one of them is lost. Receive-only RF listeners placed
elsewhere in the house (an ESPHome board with a CC1101, an RTL-SDR)
decode what they hear and publish it to MQTT; this compares what they
heard with what the modem heard and hands the modem's misses to the
protocol stack. Nothing is transmitted.

New optional `mqtt.listeners` config section. Without it nothing is
created and nothing changes. With it, Listeners:

- subscribes to decoded listener messages (default insteon-rf/msg/+):
  JSON carrying the message as the modem would have reported it
  (0x50/0x51 frame), its on-air time and receiver diagnostics;
- holds each message 2.5 s for the modem's own (often later, powerline)
  copy and does nothing if the modem heard it;
- classifies the rest into tiers (battery, group, state), never
  handling replies, the modem's own messages, unknown senders, repaired
  messages or group 0 (which raises an alert instead);
- injects listed tiers through the new Protocol.inject(), logs "shadow"
  tiers only, with per-device and global rate limits;
- publishes per-listener and per-device counters (retained) and group 0
  alerts.

Protocol gains signal_raw_read (every frame read from the modem) and
inject(), which accepts only complete 0x50/0x51 frames and ignores the
modem's own copy of an injected message for 3 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0157MSwwBp84p98F4Aq9dGR3
---
 config-example.yaml | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/config-example.yaml b/config-example.yaml
index daaf3aa..e3bd796 100644
--- a/config-example.yaml
+++ b/config-example.yaml
@@ -213,4 +213,38 @@ mqtt:
   # TO ENABLE THE DISCOVERY PLATFORM: Set the following to true
   enable_discovery: false
 
+  #==================================================================
+  # RF listeners
+  #==================================================================
+  # The modem hears only what reaches its own antenna.  Battery devices
+  # (leak, door, motion, remotes) are RF only and can't be polled, so a
+  # message the modem misses from one of them is lost.  Receive-only RF
+  # listeners elsewhere in the house (for example a LilyGO T-Embed CC1101
+  # running ESPHome, or an RTL-SDR) can publish what they decode here.
+  # Messages the modem missed are then handled as though it had heard them.
+  # Nothing is ever transmitted; the modem stays the only transmitter.
+  #
+  # Each listener publishes JSON to its own topic:
+  #   {"v": 1, "rx": "t-embed", "t": 1794759872.429,
+  #    "frame": "0250...", "copies": 3, "hops_left": 2,
+  #    "rssi": -78.5, "snr": null, "repaired": 0}
+  # where "frame" is the message as the modem would have reported it.
+  #
+  # Tiers:  battery = broadcasts and cleanups from battery devices;
+  # group = any group broadcast or cleanup; state = other messages to the
+  # modem.  Replies (ACK/NAK), the modem's own messages, unknown senders,
+  # repaired messages and group 0 broadcasts are never handled.  Tiers in
+  # "shadow" are only logged ("would inject"), so a tier can be watched
+  # before it is turned on.
+  #
+  # listeners:
+  #   topic: 'insteon-rf/msg/+'
+  #   inject: ['battery']
+  #   shadow: ['group', 'state']
+  #   # Counters per listener and per device, published retained.
+  #   stats_topic: 'insteon/listeners/stats'
+  #   stats_interval: 300
+  #   # A group 0 broadcast ("all on") heard by a listener.
+  #   alert_topic: 'insteon/listeners/alert'
+
 #----------------------------------------------------------------
